you liked frog's breath.

228
00:18:56.499 --> 00:19:00.086
Nothing's more suspicious
than frog's breath.

229
00:19:00.169 --> 00:19:05.007
Until you taste it,
I won't swallow a spoonful.

230
00:19:05.758 --> 00:19:07.927
I'm not hungry. Oops.

231
00:19:09.178 --> 00:19:11.514
You want me to starve...

232
00:19:11.597 --> 00:19:16.436
an old man like me,
who hardly has strength as it is.

233
00:19:16.519 --> 00:19:20.523
Me, to whom you owe
your very life.

234
00:19:20.606 --> 00:19:23.276
Oh, don't be silly.

235
00:19:25.278 --> 00:19:29.490
Mmm! See? Scrumptious!

236
00:19:38.041 --> 00:19:41.586
Did anyone think
to dredge the lake?

237
00:19:41.669 --> 00:19:44.213
Oh, this morning.

238
00:19:46.049 --> 00:19:49.761
- Hear that? -
Ah, what? - Shh.

239
00:19:51.721 --> 00:19:53.639
Zero!

240
00:19:56.184 --> 00:19:58.728
- Jack's back!
- Jack's back! Jack's back!

241
00:20:08.112 --> 00:20:13.326
- Where have you been?
- Call a town meeting and I'll tell everyone all about it.

242
00:20:13.409 --> 00:20:16.371
- When?
- Immediately!

243
00:20:20.875 --> 00:20:26.339
Town meeting! Town meeting!

244
00:20:26.422 --> 00:20:30.927
Town meeting tonight!

245
00:20:31.010 --> 00:20:36.391
Town meeting!
Town meeting tonight!

246
00:20:53.866 --> 00:20:56.869
Listen, everyone!

247
00:20:56.953 --> 00:21:00.873
I want to tell you
about Christmas Town.

248
00:21:04.001 --> 00:21:07.380
<i>There were objects so peculiar
they were not to be believed</i>

249
00:21:07.463 --> 00:21:10.925
<i>All around things
to tantalize my brain</i>

250
00:21:11.008 --> 00:21:14.387
<i>It's a world unlike anything
I've ever seen</i>

251
00:21:14.470 --> 00:21:17.890
<i>And as hard as I tried
I can't seem to describe</i>

252
00:21:17.974 --> 00:21:21.436
<i>Like a most improbable dream</i>

253
00:21:21.519 --> 00:21:24.939
<i>But you must believe
when I tell you this</i>

254
00:21:25.023 --> 00:21:30.403
<i>It's as real as my skull
and it does exist</i>

255
00:21:30.486 --> 00:21:33.489
Here, let me show you.

256
00:21:36.159 --> 00:21:37.577
Ooh!

257
00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:40.204
<i>This is a thing
called a present</i>

258
00:21:40.288 --> 00:21:42.248
<i>The whole thing
starts with a box</i>

259
00:21:42.331 --> 00:21:44.834
<i>- A box - Is it steel
- Are there locks</i>

260
00:21:44.917 --> 00:21:48.296
<i>- Is it filled with a pox
- A pox, how delightful, a pox</i>

261
00:21:48.379 --> 00:21:49.756
If you please.

262
00:21:49.839 --> 00:21:52.467
<i>Just a box with
bright colored paper</i>

263
00:21:52.550 --> 00:21:55.136
<i>And the whole thing's
topped with a bow</i>

264
00:21:55.219 --> 00:21:58.556
<i>- A bow - But why - How ugly
- What's in it, what's in it</i>

265
00:21:58.639 --> 00:22:00.349
<i>That's the point of the thing
Not to know</i>

266
00:22:00.433 --> 00:22:03.061
<i>- It's a bat - Will it bend
- It's a rat - Will it break</i>

267
00:22:03.144 --> 00:22:05.855
<i>Perhaps it's the head
that I found in the lake</i>

268
00:22:05.938 --> 00:22:08.441
<i>Listen now
You don't understand</i>

269
00:22:08.524 --> 00:22:12.111
<i>That's not the point
of Christmasland</i>

270
00:22:12.195 --> 00:22:15.990
<i>Now pay attention
We pick up an oversized sock</i>

271
00:22:16.074 --> 00:22:18.743
<i>And hang it like this
on the wall</i>

272
00:22:18.826 --> 00:22:20.745
<i>Oh, yes, does it still
have a foot</i>

273
00:22:20.828 --> 00:22:23.998
<i>- Let me see, let me look
- Is it rotted and covered with gook</i>

274
00:22:24.082 --> 00:22:25.708
Um, let me explain.

275
00:22:25.792 --> 00:22:28.586
<i>There's no foot inside
but there's candy</i>

276
00:22:28.669 --> 00:22:31.130
<i>- Or sometimes it's filled with small toys
- Small toys</i>

277
00:22:31.214 --> 00:22:33.508
<i>- Do they bite - Do they
snap - Or explode in the sack</i>

278
00:22:33.591 --> 00:22:36.344
<i>Well, perhaps they just spring
out and scare girls and boys</i>

279
00:22:36.427 --> 00:22:38.971
<i>What a splendid idea
This Christmas sounds fun</i>

280
00:22:39.055 --> 00:22:41.808
<i>I fully endorse it
Let's try it at once</i>

281
00:22:41.891 --> 00:22:44.310
<i>Everyone, please
Now not so fast</i>

282
00:22:44.394 --> 00:22:47.480
<i>There's something here
that you don't quite grasp</i>

283
00:22:47.563 --> 00:22:49.899
I don't know.
Do you get it?

284
00:22:49.982 --> 00:22:53.236
Well, I may as well
give them what they want.

285
00:22:53.319 --> 00:22:57.031
<i>And the best I must confess
I have saved for the last</i>

286
00:22:57.115 --> 00:23:00.493
<i>For the ruler
of this Christmasland</i>

287
00:23:00.576 --> 00:23:04.038
<i>Is a fearsome king
with a deep, mighty voice</i>

288
00:23:04.122 --> 00:23:07.500
<i>Least, that's what
I've come to understand</i>

289
00:23:07.583 --> 00:23:11.003
<i>And I've also heard it told
That he's something to behold</i>

290
00:23:11.087 --> 00:23:14.507
<i>Like a lobster huge and red</i>

291
00:23:14.590 --> 00:23:18.052
<i>When he sets out to slay
with his rain gear on</i>

292
00:23:18.136 --> 00:23:21.556
<i>Can'ting bulging sacks
with his big great arms</i>

293
00:23:21.639 --> 00:23:24.934
<i>That is so I've heard it said</i>

294
00:23:25.018 --> 00:23:28.771
<i>And on a dark cold night
under full moonlight</i>

295
00:23:28.855 --> 00:23:34.277
<i>He flies into a fog
like a vulture in the sky</i>

296
00:23:34.360 --> 00:23:37.864
<i>And they call him</i>

297
00:23:37.947 --> 00:23:43.077
<i>Sandy Claws</i>

298
00:23:47.206 --> 00:23:49.709
<i>Well, at least they're excited</i>

299
00:23:49.792 --> 00:23:52.378
<i>But they don't understand</i>

300
00:23:52.462 --> 00:23:57.050
<i>That special kind of feeling
in Christmasland</i>

301
00:23:57.133 --> 00:24:00.053
Oh, well.

302
00:24:09.771 --> 00:24:11.731
Hmm.

303
00:24:19.155 --> 00:24:21.199
Hmm.

304
00:24:32.668 --> 00:24:37.382
There's got to be a logical way
to explain this Christmas thing.

305
00:24:48.935 --> 00:24:54.524
You've poisoned me for the
last time, you wretched girl.

306
00:25:02.740 --> 00:25:06.369
Oh, my head!

307
00:25:09.163 --> 00:25:12.709
The door is open!

308
00:25:12.792 --> 00:25:16.629
- Hello!
- Jack Skellington!

309
00:25:16.713 --> 00:25:21.718
- Up here, my boy.
- Doctor, I need to borrow some equipment.

310
00:25:21.801 --> 00:25:25.471
Is that so? Whatever for?

311
00:25:25.555 --> 00:25:29.016
I'm conducting a series
of experiments.

312
00:25:29.100 --> 00:25:32.145
How perfectly marvelous!

313
00:25:32.228 --> 00:25:36.482
- Curiosity killed the cat, you know.
- I know.

314
00:25:36.566 --> 00:25:40.653
Come on into the lab
and we'll get you all fixed up.

315
00:25:40.737 --> 00:25:43.322
Hmm. Experiments?

316
00:25:46.784 --> 00:25:48.953
Zero, I'm home!

317
00:26:53.518 --> 00:26:57.980
Interesting reaction!
But what does it mean?

318
00:28:37.872 --> 00:28:42.543
You can come out now
if you promise to behave.

319
00:28:42.627 --> 00:28:46.631
Sally?

320
00:28:46.714 --> 00:28:49.926
Oh, gone again!

321
00:29:03.981 --> 00:29:06.109
Hmm.

322
00:29:53.865 --> 00:29:56.159
Oh!

323
00:30:19.098 --> 00:30:22.560
<i>Something's up with Jack
Something's up with Jack</i>

324
00:30:24.520 --> 00:30:27.607
<i>Don't know if we're ever
going to get him back</i>

325
00:30:29.692 --> 00:30:32.820
<i>He's all alone up there
locked away inside</i>

326
00:30:35.365 --> 00:30:38.117
<i>- Never says a word
- Hope he hasn't died</i>

327
00:30:38.201 --> 00:30:41.120
<i>Something's up with Jack
Something's up with Jack</i>

328
00:30:49.295 --> 00:30:52.465
<i>Christmastime
is buzzing in my skull</i>

329
00:30:52.548 --> 00:30:55.551
<i>Will it let me be
I cannot tell</i>

330
00:30:55.635 --> 00:30:58.721
<i>There's so many things
I cannot grasp</i>

331
00:30:58.805 --> 00:31:01.849
<i>When I think I've got it
and then at last</i>

332
00:31:01.933 --> 00:31:04.977
<i>Through my bony fingers
it does slip</i>

333
00:31:05.061 --> 00:31:07.689
<i>Like a snowflake
in a fiery grip</i>

334
00:31:07.772 --> 00:31:11.401
<i>Something here I'm not quite getting
Though I try I keep forgetting</i>

335
00:31:11.484 --> 00:31:14.946
<i>Like a memory
long since past</i>

336
00:31:15.029 --> 00:31:16.989
<i>Here in an instant
Gone in a flash</i>

337
00:31:17.073 --> 00:31:20.451
<i>What does it mean
What does it mean</i>

338
00:31:20.535 --> 00:31:23.830
<i>In these little bric-a-brac
A secret's waiting to be cracked</i>

339
00:31:23.913 --> 00:31:28.251
<i>These dolls and toys confuse me so
Confound it all, I love it though</i>

340
00:31:28.334 --> 00:31:32.171
<i>Simple objects, nothing more
But something's hidden through a door</i>

341
00:31:32.255 --> 00:31:37.593
<i>Though I do not have the key
Something's here I cannot see</i>

342
00:31:37.677 --> 00:31:40.346
<i>What does it mean
What does it mean</i>

343
00:31:41.431 --> 00:31:43.182
<i>What does it mean</i>

344
00:31:44.058 --> 00:31:48.438
Hmm. Hmm.

345
00:31:48.521 --> 00:31:51.399
<i>I've read these Christmas books
so many times</i>

346
00:31:51.482 --> 00:31:54.527
<i>I know the stories
and I know the rhymes</i>

347
00:31:54.610 --> 00:31:57.613
<i>I know the Christmas carols
all by heart</i>

348
00:31:57.697 --> 00:32:00.950
<i>My skull's so full
it's tearing me apart</i>

349
00:32:01.034 --> 00:32:03.995
<i>As often as I've read them
Something's wrong</i>

350
00:32:04.078 --> 00:32:07.040
<i>It's so hard to put
my bony finger on</i>

351
00:32:07.123 --> 00:32:10.626
<i>Or perhaps it's really not as deep
as I've been led to think</i>

352
00:32:10.710 --> 00:32:13.963
<i>Am I trying much too hard</i>

353
00:32:14.047 --> 00:32:15.923
<i>Of course
I've been too close to see</i>

354
00:32:16.007 --> 00:32:19.302
<i>The answer's right in front of me
Right in front of me</i>

355
00:32:19.385 --> 00:32:23.097
<i>It's simple really, very clear
Like music drifting in the air</i>

356
00:32:23.181 --> 00:32:26.726
<i>Invisible but everywhere</i>

357
00:32:26.809 --> 00:32:31.230
<i>Just because I cannot see it
Doesn't mean I can't believe it</i>

358
00:32:31.314 --> 00:32:34.859
<i>You know I think this Christmas thing
is not as tricky as it seems</i>

359
00:32:34.942 --> 00:32:38.321
<i>And why should they have all the fun
It should belong to anyone</i>

360
00:32:38.404 --> 00:32:42.158
<i>Not anyone in fact, but me
Why I can make a Christmas tree</i>

361
00:32:42.241 --> 00:32:45.620
<i>And there's no reason I can find
I couldn't handle Christmastime</i>

362
00:32:45.703 --> 00:32:51.084
<i>I bet I could improve it too
And that's exactly what I'll do</i>

363
00:32:54.170 --> 00:32:55.630
Eureka!

364
00:32:55.713 --> 00:33:00.385
This year,
Christmas will be ours!

365
00:33:04.931 --> 00:33:10.144
Patience, everyone. Jack has
a special job for each of you.

366
00:33:12.063 --> 00:33:15.358
Dr. Beetlestein.

367
00:33:15.441 --> 00:33:18.444
Your Christmas assignment
is ready.

368
00:33:20.655 --> 00:33:25.034
Dr. Beetlestein,
to the front of the line.

369
00:33:29.622 --> 00:33:32.625
What kind of noise is that
for a baby to make?

370
00:33:32.709 --> 00:33:35.461
- Perhaps it can be improved?
- No problem!

371
00:33:35.545 --> 00:33:37.338
I knew it!

372
00:33:37.422 --> 00:33:41.008
Doctor, thank you for coming.

373
00:33:41.092 --> 00:33:43.553
We need some of these.

374
00:33:43.636 --> 00:33:45.805
Hmm.

375
00:33:45.888 --> 00:33:49.475
Their construction should be
exceedingly simple, I think.

376
00:33:49.559 --> 00:33:52.979
How horrible
our Christmas will be.

377
00:33:53.062 --> 00:33:55.690
No! How jolly!

378
00:33:55.773 --> 00:33:59.736
Oh. How jolly
our Christmas will be.

379
00:34:02.613 --> 00:34:05.658
- What are you doing here?
- Jack sent for us.

380
00:34:05.742 --> 00:34:07.785
- Specifically.
- By name.

381
00:34:07.869 --> 00:34:10.538
- Lock. -
Shock. - Barrel.

382
00:34:10.621 --> 00:34:14.625
Jack, Jack,
it's Boogie's boys.

383
00:34:14.709 --> 00:34:19.213
Ah, Halloween's finest
trick-or-treaters.

384
00:34:19.297 --> 00:34:22.675
The job I have for you
is top secret.

385
00:34:22.759 --> 00:34:25.678
It requires craft,
cunning, mischief.

386
00:34:25.762 --> 00:34:28.931
And we thought
you didn't like us, Jack.

387
00:34:30.767 --> 00:34:34.270
Absolutely no one
is to know about it. Not a soul!

388
00:34:34.354 --> 00:34:36.147
Now.

389
00:34:38.274 --> 00:34:40.526
Tree.

390
00:34:41.778 --> 00:34:44.197
Christmas Town.

391
00:34:44.280 --> 00:34:47.867
Ow! Hmm.

392
00:34:47.950 --> 00:34:50.370
And one more thing.

393
00:34:50.453 --> 00:34:53.956
Leave that no-account
Oogie Boogie out of this!

394
00:34:54.040 --> 00:34:55.708
Whatever you say, Jack.

395
00:34:55.792 --> 00:34:59.879
- Of course, Jack.
- Wouldn't dream of it, Jack.

396
00:35:18.481 --> 00:35:21.859
<i>Kidnap Mr. Sandy Claws</i>

397
00:35:21.943 --> 00:35:26.989
<i>- I wanna do it - Let's draw straws
- Jack said we should work together</i>

398
00:35:27.073 --> 00:35:29.409
<i>- Three of a kind - Birds of
a feather - Now and forever</i>

399
00:35:29.492 --> 00:35:36.582
<i>La, la, la, la, la, la
La, la, la, la, la</i>

400
00:35:36.666 --> 00:35:40.211
<i>Kidnap the Sandy Claws
Lock him up real tight</i>

401
00:35:40.294 --> 00:35:43.715
<i>Throw away the key
and then turn off all the lights</i>

402
00:35:43.798 --> 00:35:47.260
<i>First we're going to set some bait
inside a nasty trap and wait</i>

403
00:35:47.343 --> 00:35:50.763
<i>When he comes a-sniffing
We will snap the trap and close the gate</i>

404
00:35:50.847 --> 00:35:54.058
<i>Wait, I've got a better plan
to catch this big red lobster man</i>

405
00:35:54.142 --> 00:35:57.729
<i>Let's pop him in a boiling pot
And when he's done we'll butter him up</i>

406
00:35:57.812 --> 00:36:01.190
<i>Kidnap the Sandy Claws
Throw him in a box</i>

407
00:36:01.274 --> 00:36:04.694
<i>Bury him for 90 years
Then see if he talks</i>

408
00:36:06.487 --> 00:36:09.949
<i>And Mr. Oogie Boogie man</i>

409
00:36:10.033 --> 00:36:13.411
<i>Can take the whole thing
over then</i>

410
00:36:13.494 --> 00:36:16.789
<i>He'll be so pleased I do declare</i>

411
00:36:16.873 --> 00:36:19.709
<i>That he will cook him rare
Whee</i>

412
00:36:25.882 --> 00:36:29.302
<i>I say that we take a cannon
Aim it at his door and then</i>

413
00:36:29.385 --> 00:36:32.972
<i>Knock three times and when he answers
Sandy Claws will be no more</i>

414
00:36:33.056 --> 00:36:36.392
<i>You're so stupid Think now if
we blow him up to smithereens</i>

415
00:36:36.476 --> 00:36:39.812
<i>We may lose some pieces and then
Jack will beat us black and green</i>

416
00:36:39.896 --> 00:36:43.191
<i>Kidnap the Sandy Claws
Tie him in a bag</i>

417
00:36:43.274 --> 00:36:46.277
<i>Throw him in the ocean
Then see if he is sad</i>

418
00:36:46.361 --> 00:36:50.323
<i>Because Mr. Oogie Boogie
is the meanest guy around</i>

419
00:36:50.406 --> 00:36:55.536
<i>- If I were on his boogie list
- I'd get out of town</i>

420
00:36:57.205 --> 00:37:00.750
<i>He'll be so pleased
by our success</i>

421
00:37:00.833 --> 00:37:04.253
<i>That he'll reward us too
I'll bet</i>

422
00:37:04.337 --> 00:37:07.673
<i>Perhaps he'll make
his special brew</i>

423
00:37:07.757 --> 00:37:09.592
<i>Of snake and spider stew</i>

424
00:37:09.675 --> 00:37:12.929
<i>We're his little henchmen
and we take our job with pride</i>

425
00:37:13.012 --> 00:37:16.474
<i>We do our best to please him
and stay on his good side</i>

426
00:37:16.557 --> 00:37:19.227
<i>- I wish my cohorts weren't so dumb
- I'm not the dumb one</i>

427
00:37:19.310 --> 00:37:21.020
<i>- You're no fun -
Shut up - Make me</i>

428
00:37:21.104 --> 00:37:24.399
<i>I've got something, listen now
This one is real good you'll see</i>

429
00:37:24.482 --> 00:37:28.027
<i>We'll send a present to his door
Upon there'll be a note to read</i>

430
00:37:28.111 --> 00:37:31.364
<i>Now in the box we'll wait
and hide until his curiosity</i>

431
00:37:31.447 --> 00:37:35.076
<i>Entices him to look inside and then
we'll have him one, two, three</i>

432
00:37:35.159 --> 00:37:38.413
<i>Kidnap the Sandy Claws
Beat him with a stick</i>

433
00:37:38.496 --> 00:37:42.041
<i>Lock him up for 90 years
See what makes him tick</i>

434
00:37:42.125 --> 00:37:45.503
<i>Kidnap the Sandy Claws
Chop him into bits</i>

435
00:37:45.586 --> 00:37:49.048
<i>Mr. Oogie Boogie
is sure to get his kicks</i>

436
00:37:49.132 --> 00:37:52.552
<i>Kidnap the Sandy Claws
See what we will see</i>

437
00:37:52.635 --> 00:37:56.180
<i>Lock him in a cage
and then throw away the key</i>

438
00:38:02.562 --> 00:38:05.940
Sandy Claws, huh?

439
00:38:12.989 --> 00:38:15.074
It goes something like this.

440
00:38:20.663 --> 00:38:22.832
How about it?
Think you can manage?

441
00:38:22.915 --> 00:38:25.334
A- one, and a-two,
and a-three, and a...

442
00:38:32.592 --> 00:38:35.845
- Next!
- Fantastic!

443
00:38:35.928 --> 00:38:39.766
Now, why don't you all practice on that,
and we'll be in great shape.

444
00:38:39.849 --> 00:38:43.353
Sally, I need your help
more than anyone's.

445
00:38:43.436 --> 00:38:46.564
You certainly do, Jack.
I had the most terrible vision.

446
00:38:46.647 --> 00:38:50.276
- That's splendid!
- No! It was about your Christmas.

447
00:38:50.360 --> 00:38:54.489
